{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnPvdbUNmwZUttSep8pW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled PARK a **SUCCESSOR**: the finding is real and I reproduced it, but the fix belongs in its own row, not this lane. The verdict is committed as `3ea5f010c` with the `WI: WI-993` and `Loop-Session` trailers.\n\n**What the reproduction showed.** I ran it as a scratch test on the dispatch test fixtures, then deleted it without committing:\n- A claimed row whose `needs` cites a pending open item reads `blocked` in the schedule.\n- `_parked_branches` lists it anyway and the dispatcher resumes it before anything else.\n- The worker is launched with the bare `BLOCKED … no worker assignment` prompt. On its exit 4 the handback closes the row partial, and the ready row behind it is never claimed.\n- That drops the claim WI-993's new §5 rule says the lane keeps. It also leaves the open item cited only by a closed row, which is the uncited-item error on trunk.\n\n**Why MINOR and not this lane's fix.**\n- **Rare path.** The kit's own `agent-resume` route reaches it only rarely: a lane has to be parked at a planned owner step with an item someone filed by hand. On that route a worker that stops for the owner is closed partial on the same tick, which §5 already allows.\n- **Not convergence-class.** The error is loud, nothing is lost (the partial close commits the work and a handback row is minted), and the Done-when doesn't name the dispatcher. Under §6 that makes it MINOR.\n- **Not high risk** in §6's sense, so ESCALATE doesn't apply.\n- **It changes an approved row.** The fix changes the dispatcher's resume behaviour, which needs its own LLR amendment and sitting. The lane's spec lists `dispatch.py` as unchanged.\n- **The gap is older than the lane.** A claimed blocked row was already possible, and the worker prompt already refused it while the dispatcher launched it.\n\n**What the successor row must do.** The parked-lane resume skips a lane whose claimed row reads `blocked`, keeps its claim, moves on to the next ready row and ends without a stall. The row amends the resume LLR and adds a `tests/test_dispatch.py` case for this.\n\nUntil that row lands, the claim copy's Trust sentence \"a claimed one draws no worker assignment\" holds for the worker prompt but not for the dispatcher.\n\nThe `012-ADJUDICATE-26b4d09.md.requested` file is left uncommitted, as the brief asked for only the verdict file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1176,"cache_read_input_tokens":181544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1176},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5137c86e-cf2b-4214-969c-76a09f60f9fd","uuid":"3fd0cab8-2162-442d-9fa4-eebb64b70d4a","timestamp":"2026-11-06T21:37:23.016Z","request_id":"req_011CgnPvdKbeugWdcg8RWVoJ"}
